<title>FRANCE: EU cuts tax on daily soft wheat, flour exports.</title>
<headline>EU cuts tax on daily soft wheat, flour exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday cut the tax applying to daily soft wheat grain exports to five Ecus per tonne from a previous level of 15 Ecus, EU grain officials said.</p>
<p>It also cut the tax applying to daily exports of soft wheat flour to seven Ecus per tonne from 20 Ecus, they said.  </p>
<p>On May 14 the European Union restored taxes on daily wheat grain and flour exports to keep a lid on domestic supplies and prices in the face of firm world prices.</p>
<p>European Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler said this week the tax could be cut soon following a fall in prices. But an EU source had said the Commission had no plans this week to lower or scrap the export tax despite lower world prices.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
